  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Bredig&rsquo;s Arc Method is used for preparation of colloidal sol&rsquo;s of less reactive metal like Au, Ag, Pt.</p><p>Ostwald process is used for preparation of nitric acid.</p><p>Van Arkel method is used&nbsp;for refining Zirconium or Titanium.</p><p>The&nbsp;Mond process&nbsp;is a method for refining nickel. The nickel oxide and impurities react with the hydrogen gas to form an impure solid nickel.</p>",
